{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22691 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Gama-Mangostin is implicated in the interaction with MIP through a series of molecular pathways that involve the enzyme 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound, which is a target of Gama-Mangostin, appears to act as a mediator in the interaction, with Gama-Mangostin directly targeting MOVP-3 or Carboxylesterase 2, both of which are subsequently targeted by the compound. The evidence suggests that Gama-Mangostin may influence the activity of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn affects MIP. The shared involvement of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One in the targeting of MIP across different pathways indicates a potential central role in the mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the compound's activity to modulate MIP, suggesting a broader pharmacological impact.",
